Translation of the read path, Translate(handleBalance(...)). Balance can never produce ErrDuplicate (the only case
that keeps its cause), so under Go semantics the set is the fresh *api.Error values (400/404/402/500) and the sentinel
api.ErrUnavailable, with NOTHING behind (*api.Error).Unwrap.
Recorded: those 5 entries, plus 34 entries behind (*api.Error).Unwrap. Not flagged: each of them is a documented
may-match under errors.Is(err, ErrDuplicate) (plan S07: values with a custom Is method anywhere in their tree -
NotFoundError[AccountID], syscall.Errno - and Unresolved values are kept); retry.ErrGaveUp is the sibling %w
operand of such a value. Plain origins without a may-match part (errShortRecord, strconv and poll errors behind
(*CorruptError).Unwrap) are correctly absent. The kept entries get no note at the 409 site, since notes are only
attached where a value would have been removed.
Inherited imprecision: NotFoundError behind "%w after %d attempts: %w" (dominance rule, see tx_ping_decl) and the
"load of escaping variable err" values of WithTx, which reach retry.Value through Do's un-narrowed Candidates
(retry_value_decl).
